{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast","id":596502,"title":"Disatisfaction with Nightmares [Beast]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-19T22:36:39-07:00","id":596502,"title":"Disatisfaction with Nightmares [Beast]","content":"I have to say, I had a strong negative reaction to Nightmares - my brain slid off them while I was trying to read 'em.<br /> <br /> They felt so <i>external</i> to the whole thing - too... intentional.<br /> <br /> Yeah, yeah, cool nightmare powers, perfectly thematic, bla bla... <i>I really don't think that Beasts should have active powers beyond Satiety expenditures and their Lair-related powers.</i><br /> <br /> If I had my druthers, Nightmares would be to your Lair as Atavisms are to your body - they wouldn't have any effect unless you call down a Lair trait, but then... well, it's the difference between the Lair being <i>there</i> and you using the Lair as a weapon.<br /> <br /> For example, Bugs Everywhere would populate your Lair with squirming <i>things</i>. When your Lair is drawn into the real world, they come with it - swarming over your target, softening them up for the final crunch and delicious slurp of their fear.<br /> <br /> As for why it works better when you have high Satiety... your Soul doesn't understand what it's like to be <i>afraid</i>. You do - you remember what it was like to have phobias, or to get freaked out by a horror movie. So when you're thinking more like a human, you can use that empathy to be more... precise. Like a scalpel compared to your Soul's battleaxe.<br /> <br /> But yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T03:29:40-07:00","id":596675,"title":"","content":"In that case... just play using Atavisms and using Lair, keeping your Beast around Low Satiety for maximum effect?<br /> <br /> Something to keep in mind - despite being the Beast's fuel stat, Satiety is actually still an Integrity equivalent. Like any of the other supernaturals, a high Integrity equivalent still means your more human like, while a low I.E. means your more monstrous. This holds true, regardless if we're talking about Humanity, Harmony, Cover, or Satiety. Low Satiety is all about the Hungers and the Beast made manifest. Meanwhile, High Satiety is more about putting the Beast to sleep and wandering in dreams, and effectively turning from a physical character into a psychic, and eventually all but a normal human at Satiety 10. Low Satiety is about feeding Hungers, High Satiety is more about being buddies with the supernatural instead.<br /> <br /> Its a shift in tone, yes. But all games do that, in a real way. High Integrity characters play much differently than Low Integrity equivalents. I think that, given your post, we're talking about a dissonance between the two play styles here. Its like the difference between playing a high Harmony werewolf instead of a low Harmony one - the two act vastly different.<br /> <br /> If your personal play style lends itself to one of the two styles, you can just play that style, while others could play the other style, or try to balance them (eek! Medium Satiety is bad!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T05:13:54-07:00","id":596737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=596675#post596675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to keep in mind - despite being the Beast's fuel stat, Satiety is actually still an Integrity equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I know it's <i>written </i>that Satiety is an integrity equivalent but...it really isn't. There's nothing in Satiety that makes you act monstrous or human-like* depending on your level, excluding Satiety 10 and 0. The hunger conditions could have solved this issue, but they don't. They help or hinder in opening Primordial pathways. Saying Satiety is an Integrity equivalent is like saying Vitae is an Integrity equivalent - sure, when you're hungry you go somewhat crazy, but that's doesn't mean it's an Integrity trait.<br /> <br /> *Appart from the very fact that you are a Begotten, but your Satiety level changes nothing. Heck having high-Satiety also means you have to act <i>even more monstrous</i> in order to feed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T06:31:10-07:00","id":596818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=596737#post596737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's nothing in Satiety that makes you act monstrous or human-like* depending on your level, excluding Satiety 10 and 0.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure there is. High Satiety and Low Satiety effect on the Atavasms (more monstrous) and Nightmares (more human-psychic effects), for instance. Ease of fulfilling Hunger at low levels versus seeking out Family Dinners to maintain your high level.<br /> <br /> Its like Werewolf's Harmony. You're supposed to fluxuate between high and low here. The difference is that, unlike Harmony, you don't hit an ideal balance at the middle - you want one of the two extremes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T06:46:25-07:00","id":596860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=596818#post596818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sure there is. High Satiety and Low Satiety effect on the Atavasms (more monstrous) and Nightmares (more human-psychic effects), for instance. Ease of fulfilling Hunger at low levels versus seeking out Family Dinners to maintain your high level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both extremes are monstrous in different ways. Seeking family dinner is often more dangerous and inhumane than low-level feeding, but low-satiety is a monster in sheep's clothing (atavisms).<br /> <br /> There's two sliders here - Ease of feeding (with easier feeding usually meaning &quot;less-monstrous&quot;) and powers (with low-Satiety usually meaning you <i>won't </i>use your dangerous, monstrous powers as often, but your atavisms being more powerful) and these two sliders balance each other at &quot;neutral monster&quot;. So you always end up being a 50% grey in mechanical terms.<br /> <br /> Humanity defines your banes, the power that these banes hold upon you and the social penalties you have with mortals.<br /> Harmony defines how often you'll go on a death-rage and shifting to one extreme or the other is bad (mechanically speaking)<br /> Wisdom defines how far your nimbus infects people.<br /> Satiety defines...which powers you'll want to use.<br /> <br /> One of these doesn't seem to fit the bill as far as &quot;Being a monster&quot; goes. I understand that Beast is a game about <i>being a creature of nightmare</i>, but I don't think the game is any different in saying Satiety is an Integrity equivalent or simply stating that Beasts don't have any Integrity equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T06:46:59-07:00","id":596861,"title":"","content":"And that's the ease of Family Dinner coming in and tainting the equation. Feeding your hunger &quot;your way&quot; requires to be much more &quot;evil&quot; at high Satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T08:32:06-07:00","id":597010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=596860#post596860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (with easier feeding usually meaning &quot;less-monstrous&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div> When it comes to Hunger, High Satiety is harder to fulfill, meaning that you're less likely to actually fill up. Requires pretty much an entire session to set up, at least! Maybe several! That's insane! Its actually really easy to maintain a low Hunger than medial or high. The simple fact of the matter is that you'll be feeding your Hunger much less often at High Satiety. Instead, your Hunger will usually be your constant source of feeding at Low Hunger.<br /> <br /> If you want to maintain high Satiety, you're going to need to generally neglect your Hunger except for the rare morsel and focus on the Family Dinner, which gives a much more reliable way of feeding through voyeuristic means that don't necessarily hurt anyone - just watching a werewolf hunt for dinner due to their all-meat diet counts, iirc. Not very monstrous.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I'd like to point out that, if you're focusing on High Satiety and Nightmares, not only do you want to interact with other supernaturals for Family Dinner, but also for learning Kinship Nightmares.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and powers (with low-Satiety usually meaning you <i>won't </i>use your dangerous, monstrous powers as often, but your atavisms being more powerful) </div> </div> </div> Actually, with how easy it is to feed your Hunger at low levels? Its easy to use a point or two of Satiety, then go feed back up to 3. If you go higher, its easy enough to spend Satiety to get back down out of the danger zone (see below). So, no. I find that its actually <i>easy</i> to use the most dangerous powers fairly frequently, then indulge my Hunger immediately in some way.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and these two sliders balance each other at &quot;neutral monster&quot;. So you always end up being a 50% grey in mechanical terms. </div> </div> </div> Except for the slight issue that you don't want to be at Satiety 4-6. Not only do you not get Atavism or Nightmare bonuses, leaving you weaker, but you're vulnerable to a Hero. The game pushes you to the extremes - either trying to maintain a Low Satiety, where you focus on Atavisms and rapidly feeding your Hunger (which, if you slip too high, you're in danger from a Hero, who likely is looking for you while you're feeding your Hunger), or try to maintain a High Satiety and focus on Nightmares and Kinship (this also prevents you from going crazy with Nightmares, since if you go crazy with them, you'll fall into the Average Zone as well as potentially drawing a Hero's attention).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humanity defines your banes, the power that these banes hold upon you and the social penalties you have with mortals. </div> </div> </div>Exactly - you're more susecptable to mystical influences and act less human at low levels. I would also like to point out that, due to the social penalties, you are more likely to fall back on Disciplines for feeding. Majesty to get rid of the penalties, Dominate or Obfuscate to bypass the need altogether, Auspex to get around the inability to read emotions well, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Harmony defines how often you'll go on a death-rage and shifting to one extreme or the other is bad (mechanically speaking) </div> </div> </div> Harmony, mechanically speaking, reflects how close you are to human flesh versus wolf spirit. It affects more than just death rages, it affects what world you're drawn into, and which form you act most like. You break towards being human by eating salad and pizza, don't forget. Acting human means we get a higher Harmony score (maybe too high).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Satiety defines...which powers you'll want to use. </div> </div> </div> And how you feed your Satiety over time. And how you spend your hours of the day - seeking out new Kinship for more Nightmares, or looking for new chances to feed your Hunger or grow your Lair. One is much more humane than the other. Harmony wants you to balance at the middle. Satiety detests balance and encourages extremes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wisdom defines how far your nimbus infects people. </div> </div> </div> Ahh... not quite. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage blog</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">High-Wisdom mages cast magic subtly and carefully, minimizing the effects of witnessing the supernatural on Sleeper\u2019s Integrity. They act with care for consequences, rather than abusing their gnosis to impose their own selfish ends. Low-Wisdom mages are direct and at times brutal with their spells, using too much power or creating indiscriminate spell effects because it\u2019s easier and faster.</span></span></span><ul><li>While Gnosis determines how overtly supernatural a mage\u2019s nimbus is, Wisdom determines how far it spreads \u2013 the lower the further.</li> <li>At permanent Wisdom 0 (not through \u201cinjury\u201d, but hubris), a character becomes one of \u201cthe Mad\u201d, a mage with a broken soul who has lost conscious control of her magic and \u201cleaks\u201d Supernal energy. Being Mad is incurable except perhaps through archmastery of Death.</li> <li>Mage characters attempting to contain a Paradox within their own pattern contest the Paradox roll by rolling Wisdom.</li> <li>High and Low Wisdom provides dice modifiers to interacting with Goetia and Supernal Entities, but not Spirits and Ghosts.&quot;</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.... So, lets review. High Wisdom mages are subtle, careful, show less obvious of a Nimbus, bonus to containing paradoxes. They look and act much more like regular people. Low Wisdom mages throw obvious magic around, their Nimbus is more obvious to observers, and paradoxes tend to happen on the outside where observers can see them. Clearly, one's more obviously a mage, a mental monster, than the other.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And lets not forget that Demon certainly still applies. High Cover, you appear more human, you have less glitches, you have more connections with people around you, a real part of society. You'll likely focus on Embeds, subtle powers, because you don't want to risk it.<br /> <br /> Low Cover means that we've got parts of your true nature showing through, you live in impossible spaces, and you have a bookshelf with only one book, repeated fifteen times, including the torn cover. Most likely worn for missions, which means we're pulling out the big guns (Exploits, demon form) which are much more obviously monster powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Satiety defines...which powers you'll want to use. </div> </div> </div> A focus on Atavisms mean you physically appear more than human. You literally fly, you loom larger than life, you are unearthly beautiful. You breath fire and cause indoor wind storms with a wave of your hands.<br /> <br /> Nightmares are freaking people out with a look or touch. Run your fingers down someone's back, and they freak out since they feel like spiders are crawling along their skin. A glare that shoots daggers makes someone scared enough that they'll listen to your commands while you're in sight. Not exactly the appearance of a monster here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of these doesn't seem to fit the bill as far as &quot;Being a monster&quot; goes. I understand that Beast is a game about <i>being a creature of nightmare</i>, but I don't think the game is any different in saying Satiety is an Integrity equivalent or simply stating that Beasts don't have any Integrity equivalent. </div> </div> </div> Its all in how they act. Remember, I'm talking about acting human, not acting humanely. There's a difference. These aren't Morality equivalents anymore. Its about a spiritual balance of some kind.<br /> <br /> Acting like a monster, no matter the game, has nothing to do with morality. You can be an exceedingly moral vampire at low Humanity. You just can't pass for human worth crap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-20-2015, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T09:26:38-07:00","id":597030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597010#post597010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you want to maintain high Satiety, you're going to need to generally neglect your Hunger except for the rare morsel and focus on the Family Dinner, which gives a much more reliable way of feeding through voyeuristic means that don't necessarily hurt anyone - just watching a werewolf hunt for dinner due to their all-meat diet counts, iirc. Not very monstrous.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly the prey has to suffer. so watching the feeding resulting from a Siskur Dah would work but ordinary hunting does not. Similarly vampires snacking on blood dolls doesn't do the trick. There has to be stalking / conquest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597010#post597010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly - you're more susecptable to mystical influences and act less human at low levels. I would also like to point out that, due to the social penalties, you are more likely to fall back on Disciplines for feeding. Majesty to get rid of the penalties, Dominate or Obfuscate to bypass the need altogether, Auspex to get around the inability to read emotions well, etc.<br /> <br /> Harmony, mechanically speaking, reflects how close you are to human flesh versus wolf spirit. It affects more than just death rages, it affects what world you're drawn into, and which form you act most like. You break towards being human by eating salad and pizza, don't forget. Acting human means we get a higher Harmony score (maybe too high).<br /> <br /> And how you feed your Satiety over time. And how you spend your hours of the day - seeking out new Kinship for more Nightmares, or looking for new chances to feed your Hunger or grow your Lair. One is much more humane than the other. Harmony wants you to balance at the middle. Satiety detests balance and encourages extremes.<br /> <br /> Ahh... not quite. Hmm.... So, lets review. High Wisdom mages are subtle, careful, show less obvious of a Nimbus, bonus to containing paradoxes. They look and act much more like regular people. Low Wisdom mages throw obvious magic around, their Nimbus is more obvious to observers, and paradoxes tend to happen on the outside where observers can see them. Clearly, one's more obviously a mage, a mental monster, than the other.<br /> <br /> And lets not forget that Demon certainly still applies. High Cover, you appear more human, you have less glitches, you have more connections with people around you, a real part of society. You'll likely focus on Embeds, subtle powers, because you don't want to risk it.<br /> <br /> Low Cover means that we've got parts of your true nature showing through, you live in impossible spaces, and you have a bookshelf with only one book, repeated fifteen times, including the torn cover. Most likely worn for missions, which means we're pulling out the big guns (Exploits, demon form) which are much more obviously monster powers.<br /> <br /> A focus on Atavisms mean you physically appear more than human. You literally fly, you loom larger than life, you are unearthly beautiful. You breath fire and cause indoor wind storms with a wave of your hands.<br /> <br /> Nightmares are freaking people out with a look or touch. Run your fingers down someone's back, and they freak out since they feel like spiders are crawling along their skin. A glare that shoots daggers makes someone scared enough that they'll listen to your commands while you're in sight. Not exactly the appearance of a monster here.<br /> <br /> Its all in how they act. Remember, I'm talking about acting human, not acting humanely. There's a difference. These aren't Morality equivalents anymore. Its about a spiritual balance of some kind.<br /> <br /> Acting like a monster, no matter the game, has nothing to do with morality. You can be an exceedingly moral vampire at low Humanity. You just can't pass for human worth crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forget, but how does Satiety affect breaking points? Do Beasts actually have breaking points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T09:46:19-07:00","id":597042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597030#post597030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly the prey has to suffer. so watching the feeding resulting from a Siskur Dah would work but ordinary hunting does not. Similarly vampires snacking on blood dolls doesn't do the trick. There has to be stalking / conquest.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not sure on the suffering prey part, but I do know that there's two parts to Family Dinner. 1) Sucessfully stalking prey down. 2) Actual feeding. Each one gets you one point of Satiety. So, watching a vampire snack on a blood doll does get one Satiety. Watching a vampire hunt someone down then feeding gives two Satiety. Hunting someone down but not feeding is one point (catch and release, possibly as a competition).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I forget, but how does Satiety affect breaking points? Do Beasts actually have breaking points? </div> </div> </div>There are not. There's only time and spending Satiety for powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T09:56:14-07:00","id":597044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597042#post597042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not sure on the suffering prey part, but I do know that there's two parts to Family Dinner. 1) Sucessfully stalking prey down. 2) Actual feeding. Each one gets you one point of Satiety. So, watching a vampire snack on a blood doll does get one Satiety. Watching a vampire hunt someone down then feeding gives two Satiety. Hunting someone down but not feeding is one point (catch and release, possibly as a competition).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The hunting is mandatory, and if they feed it's one extra. Blood dolls don't count under these conditions.<br /> <br /> As for your long (detailed and very well written) post to answer my qualms, I'll have to meditate upon your words before answering, because I don't want to answer hastily without thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T10:43:37-07:00","id":597063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast#post596502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had my druthers, Nightmares would be to your Lair as Atavisms are to your body - they wouldn't have any effect unless you call down a Lair trait, but then... well, it's the difference between the Lair being <i>there</i> and you using the Lair as a weapon.<br /> <br /> For example, Bugs Everywhere would populate your Lair with squirming <i>things</i>. When your Lair is drawn into the real world, they come with it - swarming over your target, softening them up for the final crunch and delicious slurp of their fear.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div> I must admit, while I feel Atavisms need no changes, I do like the idea you present. Some sort of powerset that strengths and enhances Lair Traits, turning imposing one into a more powerful option. Would that work as a type of Merit, or how else might something like that be done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:52:15-07:00","id":597121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597044#post597044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. The hunting is mandatory, and if they feed it's one extra. Blood dolls don't count under these conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div> True, not sure how you can have a feeding without a hunt, since its indicated it supposed to be separate, but the point remains. Watching a vampire at a sex club using Majesty to pick a random person to feed from would count as Family Dinner for feeding Satiety, or a changeling picking a (non-physical) fight to feed on anger would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T12:09:17-07:00","id":597159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597042#post597042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There are not. There's only time and spending Satiety for powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll confess that I haven't re-read the latest draft in a couple of weeks but IIRC, Beast essentially jettisons many of the core nWoD systems (e.g., integrity / breaking points, separate &quot;energy&quot; pool, among others). I wonder if this might not be the root of much of the discomfort regarding Beast as a game. To me it certainly looks like there is a dearth of conflict hooks, especially for WoD's signature &quot;personal horror&quot; aspect that all of the other games possess.<br /> <br /> Additional mechanics such as more humanesque breaking points at high satiety (suffering guilt for preying on humans with wanton abandon) and more monstrous breaking points at low satiety (suffering guilt for not glutting on a feast when presented with one of suffering an insult without punishing the transgressor) might be an interesting addition. Essentially providing the storyteller with a means to drive Beasts to the dangerous middle ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T12:10:51-07:00","id":597160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597121#post597121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> True, not sure how you can have a feeding without a hunt, since its indicated it supposed to be separate, but the point remains. Watching a vampire at a sex club using Majesty to pick a random person to feed from would count as Family Dinner for feeding Satiety, or a changeling picking a (non-physical) fight to feed on anger would.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my point. However, I thought I also recalled that the hunt had to be supernatural in nature, so running down a rabbit as a wolf or shooting an elk with a rifle wouldn't count in the case of werewolves. I may be misremembering though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T12:15:26-07:00","id":597165,"title":"","content":"You know, I'll have to agree with MCN here. They explained themselves extremely well. Your desired Satiety isn't just a decision made with dice pools in mind, or at least not for a more observant player. The Satiety you want most is reflected in little things of your routine and the sum of your activities/life experiences. It could be jokingly referred to as your Diet. If you want more &quot;muscle&quot; (mighty and brutal Atavisms) you increase your &quot;protein intake&quot; (<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>+</b></span>Satiety). If you want a more &quot;athletic&quot; build (scalpel-like Nightmares that go straight for the fear and can be explained away as the victim being insane, drugged, cowardly etc) you avoid &quot;fats&quot; (<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-</b></span>Satiety). That's how I interpreted it, at least. I might be very wrong, and appreciate it if people correct me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T12:34:52-07:00","id":597182,"title":"","content":"While I probably would play a Beast like that, MCN, I don't see myself playing Beast - the theme and mechanics don't set me on fire, let's just say (Which is fine! I'm just not the target audience.)<br /> <br /> The specific reason that I find Nightmares unsatisfying, I guess, is that they feel like spells. They feel like a mystical whammy that you try to put on someone - not like waves created by your movement through the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> While &quot;powers that MAKE FEAR&quot; is a solid one, I'd like it to feel more like I'm a big ol' monster whose breaking minds <i>because I am me</i>.<br /> <br /> Eh, if I run Beast I can probably tweak Nightmares to work the way I want them to (<i>big</i> if - I have some gripes with how certain mechanics were handled. Like how the Basilisk's Touch Atavism kills people <i>way</i> too quickly at Low Satiety, or how Cyclopean Strength's Satiety Expenditure effect breaks combat on its little knee.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T12:53:32-07:00","id":597189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597165#post597165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I'll have to agree with MCN here. They explained themselves extremely well. Your desired Satiety isn't just a decision made with dice pools in mind, or at least not for a more observant player. The Satiety you want most is reflected in little things of your routine and the sum of your activities/life experiences. It could be jokingly referred to as your Diet. If you want more &quot;muscle&quot; (mighty and brutal Atavisms) you increase your &quot;protein intake&quot; (<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>+</b></span>Satiety). If you want a more &quot;athletic&quot; build (scalpel-like Nightmares that go straight for the fear and can be explained away as the victim being insane, drugged, cowardly etc) you avoid &quot;fats&quot; (<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-</b></span>Satiety). That's how I interpreted it, at least. I might be very wrong, and appreciate it if people correct me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think it's exactly the opposite? Low Satiety = better Atavisms and High Satiety = better Nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T13:24:10-07:00","id":597201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597182#post597182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The specific reason that I find Nightmares unsatisfying, I guess, is that they feel like spells. They feel like a mystical whammy that you try to put on someone - not like waves created by your movement through the Primordial Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nightmares are the high-Satiety power because they rely on having a greater connection to the wider world \u2014 particularly Kinship Nightmares \u2014 and it's hard to effectively marshal your terrifying resources when your soul is both restless and undiscriminating. By the same token, it's hard to frame a power that works best when your Horror is settled down in language that's better suited to higher-energy disturbance of its surroundings.<br /> <br /> Beasts who stay Gorged often tend to be social hunters or prone to delegation of tasks; it's part of why so much of the mechanics for Kinship incentivize Beasts to provide patronage to less potent specimens of their cousins and so many Nightmares have their higher-spec iterations provide some boon to go with the terror \u2014 sitting further from the raw impulses of the Horror means you have more psychological/metaphysical leeway to give your fellow monsterman the gifts of fear.<br /> <br /> The other problem is that the Lair is technically part of the Horror's body and thus already covers Atavisms \u2014 Heart of the Ocean, Shadowed Soul, and Storm-Wracked are the primary exhibits here, but so is the model of gaining incongruous Atavisms through prolonged existence in a brood \u2014 whereas Nightmares largely serve to cover those aspects of being an incarnate nightmare that aren't so visceral and immediate as &quot;I breathe fire&quot; or &quot;I can plummet from the sky to strike at any time&quot; or &quot;&quot;I am a legion of awful vermin beneath a thin skin of seeming individuality.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T14:07:22-07:00","id":597300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597189#post597189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually I think it's exactly the opposite? Low Satiety = better Atavisms and High Satiety = better Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597201#post597201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Nightmares are the high-Satiety power because they rely on having a greater connection to the wider world \u2014 particularly Kinship Nightmares \u2014 and it's hard to effectively marshal your terrifying resources when your soul is both restless and undiscriminating. By the same token, it's hard to frame a power that works best when your Horror is settled down in language that's better suited to higher-energy disturbance of its surroundings.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Beasts who stay Gorged often tend to be social hunters or prone to delegation of tasks; it's part of why so much of the mechanics for Kinship incentivize Beasts to provide patronage to less potent specimens of their cousins and so many Nightmares have their higher-spec iterations provide some boon to go with the terror \u2014 sitting further from the raw impulses of the Horror means you have more psychological/metaphysical leeway to give your fellow monsterman the gifts of fear.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The other problem is that the Lair is technically part of the Horror's body and thus already covers Atavisms \u2014 Heart of the Ocean, Shadowed Soul, and Storm-Wracked are the primary exhibits here, but so is the model of gaining incongruous Atavisms through prolonged existence in a brood \u2014 whereas Nightmares largely serve to cover those aspects of being an incarnate nightmare that aren't so visceral and immediate as &quot;I breathe fire&quot; or &quot;I can plummet from the sky to strike at any time&quot; or &quot;&quot;I am a legion of awful vermin beneath a thin skin of seeming individuality.&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You are right, Jacob. I got caught up in my &quot;Diet&quot; metaphor and swapped the Satiety levels. Satchel explained the matter concisely and clearly, as he almost always does. You both get Likes.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T17:59:40-07:00","id":597576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597182#post597182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The specific reason that I find Nightmares unsatisfying, I guess, is that they feel like spells. They feel like a mystical whammy that you try to put on someone - not like waves created by your movement through the Primordial Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I think that's kinda the idea. Though, I would say more &quot;psychic attack&quot; than spell, personally, but that's just semantics. Its meant to be a completely different feeling of powers than &quot;turn into a mythological monster.&quot; You're not supposed to really feel like a dragon, or kracken, or giant with them. <br /> <br /> Personally, I also don't care for purchasing Nightmares- they just don't interest me. However, I can see how others -would- like the style to play with some character archetypes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh, if I run Beast I can probably tweak Nightmares to work the way I want them to (<i>big</i> if - I have some gripes with how certain mechanics were handled. Like how the Basilisk's Touch Atavism kills people <i>way</i> too quickly at Low Satiety, or how Cyclopean Strength's Satiety Expenditure effect breaks combat on its little knee.) </div> </div> </div> People really get in a knot over Cyclopean Strength and the like. Really, its not more powerful than Vigor, and a werewolf wins most battles with the aid of Brutal Killer and the various &quot;My claws deal +8L damage&quot; stuff you can pile on. Basilisk's Touch isn't much better, especially when we're talking about games with critters that shrug off poison. Rival Beasts can have poison immunity from their Lairs, after all, and I think most supernaturals. Really, this isn't more powerful than a Ventrue using Dominate 1 power to inflict the Mesmerize condition. <br /> <br /> I blame not being used to the power jump of 2e. If anything, I'd argue that Beasts are actually one of the weaker splats when it comes to combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T20:48:15-07:00","id":597799,"title":"","content":"The issue with Cyclopean Strength is that there's nothing that I have seen that prevents automatic successes from meaning that you succeed regardless of what you roll. If I've been missing something, I will <i>happily</i> accept that.<br /> <br /> But as it stands, the Satiety benefit of Cyclopean Strength means you <i>automatically hit</i>. Regardless of your opponent's Defense, or any penalties you might be suffering.<br /> <br /> That's what I mean by &quot;breaks combat over its knee&quot; - it circumvents Defense entirely, meaning that the guy you're fighting has to Dodge if they want to not get smacked for large amounts of damage. And Dodging means that they're locked down - so Cyclopean Strength is a bit overly strong.<br /> <br /> As for your arguments about Basalisk's Touch... other Beasts can't develop immunity to the Poisoned Tilt through their Lairs (Lair traits are all Environmental Tilts - Poisoned is Personal.) Of the other splats, I know that Werewolves can shed Tilts (I think there's one power for it, somewhere), and Demons can shed Tilts by entering Demon Form.<br /> <br /> My main issue, though, is that by dealing [Lair] damage a turn, you're essentially doing an end run around &quot;no multiple attacks&quot; by dealing damage <i>comparable</i> to attacks automatically. Also, your Poison is <i>ultra-potent</i> in combat, and then long lasting as soon as you get out. That feels... weird to me (unless your poison is Mythralgrain? I guess?).<br /> <hr /><br /> Dudeness, I started playing NWoD <i>with</i> 2e. <i>That's</i> my standards of power.<br /> <br /> And, mostly, Beasts don't hold a patch to Uratha (they do match Vampires, though - having ready access to Aggravated damage out of the gate does do that - there are some <i>nasty</i> synergies that you can get out of Atavisms.) It's just that there are some things that, as far as I can tell, break the actual math of the system.<br /> <br /> I think Beasts were ultimately kinda boring to me because, unlike the finely tuned stack of Gifts you've got in Werewolf, or the knife-blade elegance of Disciplines, most of their stuff feels... clunky. It's stuff for Spikes, not Melvins. It almost feels like the mechanics of a (really well done) fan line compared to how tight Vampire and Werewolf were, and how tight Mage looks like its shaping up to be (granted, that's the <i>precise opposite</i> of &quot;insulting with faint praise&quot; - the other gamelines set the bar REALLY high).<br /> <br /> But I think I'm going to wash my hands of the subject - no point complaining about something you're sure you don't like a priori. I'll still reply if anyone wants to continue this line of conversation (<i>especially</i> if you're a dev telling me that I've been reading effects that add automatic successes wrong. That would make me a happy duckling), I just won't start or reply to any other threads about Beast - it's just not my game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T23:41:42-07:00","id":597973,"title":"","content":"I think your point stands, it's a pretty impressive power, but there is another workaround you didn't mention- higher initiative and speed.<br /> <br /> If you're faster than the giant, then you can either pop him in the mouth and then move out of his range before he gets to act, or move out of his range and then shoot him.<br /> <br /> Then the giant will either have to either throw something, if there's anything around to throw, and if there isn't any cover that can completely protect you, shoot you in which case he's not getting any strength bonuses anyway, or chase after you to catch you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T03:14:32-07:00","id":598121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597799#post597799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with Cyclopean Strength is that there's nothing that I have seen that prevents automatic successes from meaning that you succeed regardless of what you roll. If I've been missing something, I will <i>happily</i> accept that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Armor, out running, teleporting, turn into mist/swams/ephemeral, minions getting in the way, using mind control power to make them stop fighting, stealth/invisibility, super regeneration, use environmental tilts or cover.<br /> <br /> WoD combat isn't designed to work in a D&amp;D fair fight style. Its supposed to be violent and deadly. <br /> <br /> But, obviously, you don't like the game, so there is no point in continuing this. Take care, and have fun gaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T04:41:37-07:00","id":598155,"title":"","content":"You know, just for the hells of it....<br /> <br /> Giant versus Everyone Else!<br /> We're going to take a Beast with Cyclopean Strength and Limb from Limb, versus random other supernaturals. I know that white rooms are unrealistic, but we'll just go with it for now, because I'm just here to have fun. To be really nice, we'll let the Giant go first, assuming 3 Satiety for the extra damage from Low Satiety effect of Limb from Limb (otherwise, its too lopsided). Starting Characters, Giant starting with Lair 2<br /> <br /> <u><b>Giant versus Invictus Ventrue</b></u><br /> Turn 1 Giant: *Activates both Atavisms* *Attacks the Ventrue* <br /> Ventrue suffers an Arm or Leg Wreck, and about 6 agg damage, negated some by a dot of Resilience.<br /> Turn 1 Ventrue: *Uses Dominate 1*<br /> Combat over. Subsequent turns are used to feed the Beast vitae, fully blood bonding him over the scene. <br /> Winner - Ventrue<br /> <br /> <u><b>Giant versus Gauru-form Rahu</b></u><br /> Turn 1 Giant: *Activates both Atavisms* *Attacks the Rahu*<br /> Our Rahu had the fortune to have the Fortified Form and Relentless Assult merits, which granted armor, lowering the damage from the attack by 3. Gauru heals the Tilt. We're looking at 13 health for the Werewolf, due to Full Moon 2 and Gauru form. Suffer 3 agg.<br /> Turn 1 Rahu: *Attacks* The werewolf deals, 3 damage, lets say lethal. *Activates Aspect* I see nothing that suggests the Aspect takes an action to activate.<br /> Turn 2 Giant: Now, we have a problem - we're down to our last Satiety, and suffering from the Submissive Condition. Even if we get around the Condition, we will be unable to deal agg after this turn. <br /> Turn 2 Rahu: *Attacks again for more lethal damage*<br /> Turn 3: We're out of Satiety, and we can't deal enough damage a turn to get through the armor and 7 remaining health in one turn. The wolf has no problems hitting the Giant.<br /> Combat Over.<br /> Winner - Werewolf<br /> <br /> On a side note, some of you may say &quot;Oh, you could have given the Giant more Satiety!&quot; To which, I say that we'd be dealing 2 less damage a turn. That would make this battle even more lopsided in the Werewolf's favor. <br /> <br /> <u><b>Giant versus non-Loud demon form Unchained</b></u><br /> Between armor, multiple images, and Just Bruised, the Giant will be dealing crap for damage. We can also teleport and shoot the Giant from anywhere we want with Hellfire. No contest.<br /> Winner - Unchained<br /> <br /> <b><u>Giant versus Mage</u></b><br /> Not sure how the Awakened fight yet, but we're looking at enhanced magical armors again at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T02:40:03-07:00","id":599136,"title":"","content":"I have to assume that the vinculum doesn't work like that, otherwise call to serve is a damn useless power.<br /> <br /> Why spend the experience to get a third level coil that allows you to spend 5 blood points to blood bond someone in a minute if you can blood bond someone with three turns and three vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T02:49:10-07:00","id":599138,"title":"","content":"Is usually asumed the drinks must be in separate days.<br /> <br /> Also, Dominate is a power that's not reliably used once combat started, so the Giant going first... not seeing the Ventrue pulling it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T05:20:00-07:00","id":599237,"title":"","content":"Its been confirmed that, for establishing a blood bond in 2e, all you need is three separate dirinks, no need to space them out over days. So, you could establish a bond over the course of a single scene with three drinks a few minutes apart. Sure, in character, lots of vamps assume it needs to be spread out, but this is just a mental exercise for the fun of it. The entire thing is in a meaningless, contual void.<br /> <br /> Call to Serve's advantage is to establish a tier 3 blood bond in one drink - relevant, say, in combat and your enemy likes biting. Anytime you are in a hurry, or trying to trick some with &quot;oh, its just one drink, what is the worst that can happen?&quot;<br /> <br /> Dominate 1 works great in combat. The Mesmerized Condution ends if the target takes any damage, but in a one-on-one situation? Its a combat ender. And there has never been a rule that you can't use Dominate 1 in combat; higher levels, sure, but never 1. Its actually rather reliable, even if the ST gives a penalty - Atribute+skill+discipline v Attribute+2 Lair will do that.<br /> <br /> If you're really opposed to Dominate, then just have a PC that is using obfuscate to wander out of Beast range, shoot with a gun, then turn invisible again, wander far off, shoot again, etc. Vigor-enhanced weaponry attack for +6 automatic damage on an attack versus the beast's +4. Celerity for another hit-and-run tactic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-22-2015, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T06:21:41-07:00","id":599288,"title":"","content":"Dominate is great until you're facing a group of enemies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T09:31:57-07:00","id":599506,"title":"","content":"The whole point of the exercise is 1 on 1 contextless white-room fight. 3 mortals with chainsaws can also kill just about any supers but that's not the point right now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T15:14:19-07:00","id":599862,"title":"","content":"Well... I'm just saying, good villains don't fight fair (they also lead from the rear and/or run away when thinks start looking bleak for their side). (Obvious exception for Darth Vader.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T16:49:47-07:00","id":599985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=597799#post597799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think I'm going to wash my hands of the subject - no point complaining about something you're sure you don't like a priori. I'll still reply if anyone wants to continue this line of conversation (<i>especially</i> if you're a dev telling me that I've been reading effects that add automatic successes wrong. That would make me a happy duckling), I just won't start or reply to any other threads about Beast - it's just not my game.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, how do you think these &quot;Lair Trait Atavisms&quot; idea of yours be written out as a power? Just curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T10:13:40-07:00","id":600685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596502-disatisfaction-with-nightmares-beast?p=599985#post599985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, how do you think these &quot;Lair Trait Atavisms&quot; idea of yours be written out as a power? Just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's just it. The Lair Traits generally already exist for any kind of environmental ability, while Atavisms generally cover the more personal Tilts or Conditions. To use the OP's example of Bugs Everywhere, we have the Major Traits of Diseased and Toxic, which reproduce the effects of the Nightmare in question, bugs swarming over people and making them sick. We can even expand to include things like Engulfed and Razored if we wanted to. Reproduce You Must Obey? That's just using fear to push someone around - hard leverage through Social Maneuvers, and there's several Atavisms that work to that effect. Limb From Limb does most of the same stuff as Behold! My True Form!<br /> <br /> The OP basically just wanted to get rid of Nightmares because of personal dislike. Which is fair enough - he's well within his rights as an ST to make that house rule (or, as a player, just play the Low Satiety I described above). The problem is that any attempt to turn them into an Atavism or Lair Trait is just reinventing the wheel. Now, I'm not saying we won't see more Atavisms and Lair Traits in the future, just that there's a lot of overlap. The big difference between Atavism/Lair stuff and Nightmares? The former transforms the Beast and the environment, the latter directly attacks someone else - we're basically approaching the same things from two different sides. And when you try to translate one side to the other, they're basically just reproducing stuff.<br /> <br /> So, in conclusion, there's really not much that can be done, other than making a new Trait or Atavism or two. The way the OP wants to play is already there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-23-2015, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}